## Decisions not spelled out in the plan
- The `now()` value is captured once per `allow`/`remaining` call and used both for pruning and (in `allow`) as the recorded timestamp, so a clock tick mid-call can't split the window inconsistently.
- Events at the boundary are excluded by `t > cutoff`; nothing else was needed beyond the exact spec (e.g., no integer validation beyond "below 1").

